<title>USA: FPA Medical Q4 shr loss $1.01 after charges.</title>
<headline>FPA Medical Q4 shr loss $1.01 after charges.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO, Calif. 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>FPA Medical Management Inc and Subsidiaries</p>
<p>			   Consolidated Statements of Operations</p>
<p>				 Three Months Ended December 31</p>
<p>				    1996		  1995</p>
<p> Operating revenue    $ 151,047,589	$  56,760,425</p>
<p>Income (loss)</p>
<p>    from operations     (26,332,517)	   1,538,008</p>
<p> Net income		 (23,509,318)	     676,839</p>
<p>Net income (loss)</p>
<p>    per share		     (1.01)		  0.04</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>    shares outstanding   23,199,195	   16,961,698</p>
<p>				  Year Ended December 31</p>
<p>				    1996		  1995</p>
<p>Operating revenue     $440,318,613	 $ 168,351,482</p>
<p>Income (loss)</p>
<p>    from operations    (10,589,182)	    8,125,931</p>
<p>Net income (loss)	(15,716,426)	    3,833,965</p>
<p>Net income (loss)</p>
<p>    per share		    (0.72)		   0.28</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>    shares outstanding  21,702,786	    13,693,193</p>
<p>NOTES: Net income (loss) per share and weighted average shares reflect one-for-one stock dividend effective April 3, 1995, record March 1, 1995.</p>
<p>Q4 weighted average shares outstanding 23,199,195 vs 16,961,698 includes the effect of pooling with Sterling Healthcare Group.</p>
<p>Net income for the fourth quarter 1996 was $4.2 million or $0.18 per share, excluding non-recurring charges of $36.3 million related to transaction costs associated with acquisition of Foundation Health affiliated medical centers in Arizona and California, Sterling Healthcare, and certain restructuring charges.</p>
